      {
        "base": "https://www.wananga.com/feed/rss2",
        "language": null,
        "type": "text/html",
        "value": "<div>\n  <h3>\n    <span>\n      <span>\n        \n            Kaik\u014dkiri - Manaaki Whenua\n           \n      </span>\n    </span>\n    <span>\n      \n           - CLOSED\n          \n    </span>\n  </h3>\n  <h5>\n    <span>\n      \n           Location: \u014ctaki | Full-time | Fixed-Term: Ends 31 Dec 2026\n          \n    </span>\n  </h5>\n</div>\n<div>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           Te W\u0101nanga o Raukawa is seeking a committed and highly organised\u00a0\n          \n    </span>\n    <strong>\n      \n           Kaik\u014dkiri\n          \n    </strong>\n    <span>\n      \n           \u00a0to support the operations of\u00a0\n          \n    </span>\n    <strong>\n      \n           Te Whare Manaaki Whenua\n          \n    </strong>\n    <span>\n      \n           \u00a0\u2014 the whare responsible for guiding and supporting kaupapa related to whenua, taiao, and physical infrastructure across the W\u0101nanga.\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <br />\n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           This key role involves delivering high-quality administration, upholding tikanga, and ensuring all mahi reflects the values of our kaupapa M\u0101ori institution.\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <br />\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <strong>\n      \n           We\u2019re looking for someone who:\n          \n    </strong>\n  </p>\n  <ul>\n    <li>\n      <span>\n        \n            Has proven administrative experience and is confident using Microsoft Office 365\n           \n      </span>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <span>\n        \n            Communicates clearly in both te reo M\u0101ori and English\n           \n      </span>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <span>\n        \n            Is detail-focused, organised, and builds strong working relationships\n           \n      </span>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <span>\n        \n            Can manage competing demands while meeting deadlines\n           \n      </span>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <span>\n        \n            Is committed to ongoing study and personal development\n           \n      </span>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <span>\n        \n            Upholds the values of Whakatupuranga Rua Mano and Te W\u0101nanga o Raukawa\n           \n      </span>\n    </li>\n  </ul>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           You\u2019ll be responsible for coordinating hui, maintaining accurate records and systems, and providing essential support to the Kaihaut\u016b and Kaiwhakahaere to help advance the work of Te Whare Manaaki Whenua.\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <br />\n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <strong>\n      \n           Applications close: Friday 11 July 2025\n          \n    </strong>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <br />\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           For further information or to apply for this role, please contact:\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           \u00a0\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           Dionne Seng, Kaihaut\u016b Te Whare Tiaki Rawa\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           \u012am\u0113ra:\u00a0\n          \n    </span>\n    <a href=\"mailto:dionne.seng@twor-otaki.ac.nz\" target=\"_blank\">\n      \n           dionne.seng@twor-otaki.ac.nz\n          \n    </a>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           Waea: 06 3649011\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <br />\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <br />\n    </span>\n  </p>\n</div>"
      }
    ],
